      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Slow growth calcium hydroxide apexification may be clinically impractical in some instances. This case report describes a technique and rationale for single-step use of tricalcium phosphate as an apical plug in an immature permanent root. This method permitted immediate canal obturation and placement of the permanent coronal restoration. A 7-yr follow-up confirmed that this type of apexification could be successful."},
